			<div class="content" id="post-content-1461705">
									

<p>I think this is way too extreme a containment. Since knowing that 1663 exist without knowing what it is doesn't produce the effect (and it doesn't, or else everyone who would read the main page would be affected), containment procedures similar to those of <a href="/scp-370">SCP-370</a> should work reasonably well.</p>
<p>I also dislike how it's handled out-of-character; I would've preferred the current main page to be a splash page, and the current supplemental page to be the main page.</p>
<p>Also, the effect itself is boring as atheist's hell.</p>
<p>And why would they assign the same number to the site and to the object, in-character? Clearly there are people who are authorized to know about site's existence without being authorized to know what is actually kept there.</p>

