<p>Description: SCP-1663 is a 0.1&#160;m x 0.1&#160;m x 0.1&#160;m concrete cube.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>From what I got out of it, that still wouldn't work. It's even knowing the current identification of it that would trigger; if you were to walk up to a random, rural Chinese villager and say &quot;This coin is worth trei deustche mark&quot; and the guy would smile, nod&#8230; And within a couple of weeks be burning down the whole village out of revulsion. The same thing here, &quot;SCP-1663 is a block of cement&quot; would be just as effective as &quot;SCP-1663 is a coin that&#8230;&quot; because you know its NAME. Hence, the unconventional name.</p>

